            <ArticleTitle>Aurora Kinase B Phosphorylates Histone H3.3 at Serine 31 during Mitosis in Mammalian Cells.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2042-2045</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0022-2836(17)30057-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jmb.2017.01.016</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Serine 31 of histone H3.3 is phosphorylated during mitosis in mammalian cells and has been shown to influence chromosome segregation. We established a screening system to identify candidate kinase(s) phosphorylating H3.3S31 by using siRNA library targeting 720 human kinases, and we confirmed the results with an independent kinase inhibitor screen. Aurora kinase B was the best candidate hit in both screens. Moreover, the kinase activity of Aurora B on H3.3S31 was biochemically confirmed with nucleosomal substrates in vitro.</AbstractText>
